How to add a new kernel usermode-linux for Network-In! computers
------------------------------------------------------

A) Stage 1 : get usermode kernel 
-----------
When get a kernel, get also modules
Create a directory named with the version number of the kernel.
Put into the directory the executable kernel called linux.uml


B) Stage 2 : create the modules image
-----------
Create a new file disk called modules.img in the directory :
dd if=/dev/zero of=modules.img bs=1M count=150
mkfs.ext4 modules.img
mount -o loop modules.img /mnt


E) Stage 3 : time control creation
-----------
Create time control file with the command :
stat -c %Y modules.img > modules.time
